sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Arachnoidiscus ehrenbergii Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 242 nm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 79.4/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1 weighted score 79.4/100. The script implements Schnakenberg kinetics and the Turing fastest-mode wavenumber, with sigma(k_c)=0.2415 and an equal-diffusion analytic control at -0.9649. The rendered GIF is 12 frames at 640x480 and scores cv_sim_similarity 82.2 against the gallery photograph. The nonlinear FFT peak is 284.76 nm, not 242 nm. There is no diffusivity sweep, no simulated ablation trajectory, and no specimen radial-spectrum goodness-of-fit. Those are the Pass 2 remediations. Overall 79.4/100 (faithfulness 76.4, reproducibility 86.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 76, Parameter expressivity 64, Morphometric validation 70, Source and data traceability 86, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/arachnoidiscus_ehrenbergii_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-arachnoidiscus-ehrenbergii-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/png, 682492 B, 1344×984 px, artifact_sha256 532b558687049ac74911303e8e4ec2f00cf5897a71fabf4ebebdc96cdbb2967a (sha256 532b558687049ac74911303e8e4ec2f00cf5897a71fabf4ebebdc96cdbb2967a), spec_fingerprint b07ded5023e298aa1e3dae2441f5d4048c6af5aced8dc330bdf0d572210e67a6. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: b07ded5023e298aa1e3dae2441f5d4048c6af5aced8dc330bdf0d572210e67a6; artifact_sha256: 532b558687049ac74911303e8e4ec2f00cf5897a71fabf4ebebdc96cdbb2967a. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a diffusion-driven instability selects a finite wavenumber when the inhibitor diffuses sufficiently faster than the activator. | Schnakenberg 1979: the two-species mass-action system du/dt = a - u + u^2 v, dv/dt = b - u^2 v has a stable homogeneous fixed point that can be Turing-unstable. | Sumper 2002 and Lenoci & Camp 2008: diatom biosilica nanopatterns are consistent with polyamine phase separation inside the silica deposition vesicle. | Yendo & Akatsuka 1910: Arachnoidiscus ehrenbergii was observed alive forming auxospores, so the species is extant (Holocene, 0 Ma).; reconstructed_in_script: Slot-3118 coefficients a=0.062, b=1.35, D_v/D_u=31.18 chosen so the analytic fastest mode equals the assigned 242 nm detail scale on a 6-wavelength Neumann patch. A 3-arm logarithmic spiral biases the initial condition. The GIF is the unguided activator passed through the gallery photograph's colour quantiles.; transfer_boundary: 242 nm is the campaign detail-scale assignment (tier 2_macromolecular_100nm), not a pore spacing measured on A. ehrenbergii in the cited papers. | The gallery JPEG is a stylized 100 μm frame, about 413 times coarser than 242 nm. The Wikimedia file is Arachnoidiscus sp., not a confirmed ehrenbergii type.; does_not_claim: That the three saturated spots are a measured cribral lattice, that 284.76 nm equals 242 nm, or that the gallery spiral was predicted ab initio.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Re-score as audit-v2 after those measurements exist. Do not treat the analytic-versus-eigenvalue correlation as a specimen fit.",
            "remediation needed: Run a simulated equal-diffusion ablation from the same initial condition and report the contrast ratio against the patterned trajectory.",
            "remediation needed: Segment the gallery photograph and the Wikimedia valve (Otsu foreground, coherency, radial spectrum) and report Pearson r, RMSE and KS against the rendered field, with value not equal to the reference.",
            "remediation needed: Separate the linear 242 nm carrier from the nonlinear spot spacing (Pass 1 FFT peak was 284.76 nm) and raise specimen-spectrum Pearson above 0.98 without claiming the gallery resolves 242 nm.",
            "remediation needed: Sweep D_v/D_u across the discriminant onset and show that sigma(k_c) and the nonlinear wavelength respond monotonically; put the sweep on the comparison figure." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.794"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (Pass 1 single-assessor cloud loop; no independent second model was invoked)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://x.ai> .
}

